1
00:00:37,617 --> 00:00:41,717
DO YOU HEAR MY APPEAL?

2
00:00:41,925 --> 00:00:45,925
IN MY SEVERE TRIBULATION AND DISRESS

3
00:00:46,083 --> 00:00:50,083
DO YOU HEAR MY GRON,

4
00:00:50,357 --> 00:00:54,357
MY AGONY AND MY CRYING?

5
00:00:54,675 --> 00:00:58,475
GLAD TIDING TO MY NATION,

6
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:03,020
THEY RAISED TO THE RANK OF MARTYRS,

7
00:01:03,152 --> 00:01:07,252
MY CONDOLENCES ARE NOT TO THEM,

8
00:01:07,348 --> 00:01:11,548
BUT RATER FOR THE MUSLIMS

9
00:01:11,592 --> 00:01:15,692
DO YOU HEAR MY GRON,

10
00:01:15,858 --> 00:01:19,839
MY AGONY AND MY CRYING?

11
00:01:20,021 --> 00:01:23,840
GLAD TIDING TO MY NATION,

12
00:01:24,157 --> 00:01:25,957
THEY RAISED TO THE RANK OF MARTYRS,

13
00:01:26,099 --> 00:01:28,113
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

14
00:01:28,935 --> 00:01:34,900
اَلْحَمْدُ لله وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

15
00:01:37,167 --> 00:01:45,407
We'll carry on with, the Jihad(جهاد) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه, with Muhammadﷺ,

16
00:01:46,383 --> 00:01:49,883
we talked about the Battle of Badr(بدر), move on to the Battle of Uhud(أحد).

17
00:01:51,899 --> 00:01:55,388
Uhud(أحد), started out as a victory for the Muslims,

18
00:01:57,688 --> 00:02:00,742
the army of Al-Mushrikeen(ألْمُشْرِكِين) was running away

19
00:02:03,128 --> 00:02:11,608
but because of the disobedience of the few, the whole suffered.

20
00:02:13,951 --> 00:02:18,255
Rasool Allah ﷺ has appointed, fifty archers to stay on the hill and not to move from their place.

21
00:02:18,366 --> 00:02:24,453
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Even if you see birds eating from our dead bodies, vultures eating from our dead bodies,

22
00:02:24,547 --> 00:02:26,554
DO NOT come down, until I tell you!

23
00:02:27,359 --> 00:02:31,520
And if you see us winning DO NOT come down, until I tell you! Very clear orders.

24
00:02:32,678 --> 00:02:37,583
But forty of the fifty, disobeyed those orders of Rasool Allah ﷺ and they came down from the mountains,

25
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,153
 because they thought that the battle is over.

26
00:02:40,594 --> 00:02:47,006
That’s when Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد), with his eyes of an eagle caught, the weak spot

27
00:02:47,788 --> 00:02:52,439
and he made his move and he attacked the Muslims from behind.

28
00:02:53,208 --> 00:02:55,807
So the victory was turned into a defeat.

29
00:02:57,665 --> 00:03:01,917
Rasool Allah ﷺ very swiftly changed his plan

30
00:03:02,679 --> 00:03:06,731
and he retreated up, the Mountain of Uhud(أحد),

31
00:03:07,226 --> 00:03:12,540
and he went into some of the crevices, the cracks into the mountain.

32
00:03:13,301 --> 00:03:18,557
And He climbed up, thus protecting the rest of the Muslim army

33
00:03:19,446 --> 00:03:23,103
and the Mushrikeen(ألْمُشْرِكِين) of the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), did not pursue them, any further.

34
00:03:25,003 --> 00:03:33,525
However, there was a rumor that went around that, Ibn Qami'a(إبْن قَمِئه) has killed Rasool Allah ﷺ.

35
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:36,663
He claimed that, he has killed Rasool Allah ﷺ,

36
00:03:37,503 --> 00:03:40,034
in fact, he injured Rasool Allah ﷺ.

37
00:03:41,791 --> 00:03:49,383
So, Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) wants to know the facts.

38
00:03:50,625 --> 00:03:59,784
So, he goes up a bit in the mountain and he screams, or shouts.

39
00:04:00,177 --> 00:04:00,668
He says:

40
00:04:00,724 --> 00:04:02,304
أَ فِي الْقَوْمِ محمد ؟

41
00:04:04,388 --> 00:04:06,078
Is Muhammad(محمد) among you?

42
00:04:06,709 --> 00:04:08,935
Because now, the Muslims were hiding,

43
00:04:11,236 --> 00:04:12,773
أَ فِي الْقَوْمِ محمد ؟

44
00:04:14,311 --> 00:04:15,407
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

45
00:04:15,431 --> 00:04:16,231
 لَا تُجِيْبُوْا

46
00:04:16,372 --> 00:04:17,772
Do not respond back!

47
00:04:19,724 --> 00:04:20,625
He then said:

48
00:04:21,146 --> 00:04:24,023
أَ فِي الْقَوْمِ اِبْنِ اَبِىْ قُحَافَهْ ؟

49
00:04:24,550 --> 00:04:26,408
He used to call Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) Ibn Abi Quhafa(ابن ابي قحافه),

50
00:04:26,524 --> 00:04:30,500
the nickname of his father was Abi Quhafa(ابي قحافه).

51
00:04:31,742 --> 00:04:35,143
He said: Is Abu Bakr(أبوبكر) among you?

52
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:37,363
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

53
00:04:37,811 --> 00:04:38,574
لَا تُجِيْبُوْا

54
00:04:38,598 --> 00:04:39,598
Do not respond back!

55
00:04:40,669 --> 00:04:41,174
He said:

56
00:04:41,198 --> 00:04:43,072
أَ فِي الْقَوْمِ عمرابن الخطاب ؟

57
00:04:44,298 --> 00:04:46,522
Rasool Ullah said: Do not answer back.

58
00:04:48,276 --> 00:04:49,938
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) then said:

59
00:04:50,666 --> 00:04:54,043
اِنَّ هَؤلآءِ قُتِلُوْا فَلَوْ كَانُوْا اَحْيَاء لَأَجَابُوْا

60
00:04:54,546 --> 00:04:56,077
These men have been killed,

61
00:04:56,704 --> 00:04:59,123
 if they were alive they would have responded back.

62
00:05:02,153 --> 00:05:04,511
Why did Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) only asked about only these three.?

63
00:05:06,555 --> 00:05:15,875
Because he and the Kuffar(كفار) recognized that these are the pivots of the society of the Muslim community.

64
00:05:16,605 --> 00:05:20,973
Rasool Allah ﷺ and Al-Wazeerain(ألْوَزِيْرَيْن), his two advisors,

65
00:05:22,246 --> 00:05:24,819
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and Umar رضي الله عنهما.

66
00:05:26,143 --> 00:05:32,564
And this shows you the status of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and Umar(عُمَر) wasn’t only recognized in Muslim community

67
00:05:32,603 --> 00:05:35,745
 but it was also recognized among Al-Mushrikeen(ألْمُشْرِكِين).

68
00:05:38,328 --> 00:05:41,335
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) heard that statement he couldn’t hold back.

69
00:05:42,337 --> 00:05:43,102
He said:

70
00:05:43,822 --> 00:05:48,022
 كَذَّبْتَ يَا عَدُوْاَلله اَبْقَى الله عَلَيْكَ مَا  يُخْزِيْكَ

71
00:05:48,849 --> 00:05:53,939
You are lying, you enemy of Allah the ones, who're mentioned are alive, to upset you.

72
00:05:58,539 --> 00:05:59,938
So, Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said:

73
00:06:00,461 --> 00:06:01,702
أُعْلُوْا هُبَلْ

74
00:06:02,005 --> 00:06:07,182
Raise Hubal(هبل), Hubal(هبل) is one of their many gods.

75
00:06:07,855 --> 00:06:08,961
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

76
00:06:09,005 --> 00:06:10,105
أَلَا تُجِيْبُوْا؟

77
00:06:10,169 --> 00:06:11,701
Aren’t you going to respond back?

78
00:06:12,021 --> 00:06:13,054
They said: What should we say?

79
00:06:13,094 --> 00:06:14,011
He said: Say,

80
00:06:14,178 --> 00:06:16,171
اَلله اَعْلى وَ اَجَلْ

81
00:06:16,358 --> 00:06:19,758
Allah is Higher and Greater!

82
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,306
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) said:

83
00:06:22,639 --> 00:06:24,839
اَلْعُزَّى لَنَا وَلَاعُزَّى لَكُمْ

84
00:06:25,290 --> 00:06:27,440
We have Uzza(عُزَّه) and, you have no Uzza(عُزَّه).

85
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:29,401
Uzza(عُزَّه) is another of their gods.

86
00:06:30,310 --> 00:06:31,465
Muhammadﷺ said:

87
00:06:31,517 --> 00:06:32,462
أَلَا تُجِيْبُوْا؟

88
00:06:32,891 --> 00:06:34,354
Aren’t you going to respond back?

89
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:35,612
They said: What should we say?

90
00:06:35,886 --> 00:06:36,589
He said: Say,

91
00:06:36,613 --> 00:06:39,114
اَللهُ مَوْلَانَا، وَلَامَوْلَى لَكُمْ

92
00:06:40,083 --> 00:06:42,852
Allah is our protector and, you have no protector.

93
00:06:44,929 --> 00:06:46,222
And then Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said:

94
00:06:47,318 --> 00:06:52,102
يَوْمٌ بِيَوْمِ بَدْرَ وَلَأ يَّامُ دُوَّلْ وَالْحَرْبُ سَجَالْ

95
00:06:54,035 --> 00:06:57,363
 وَسَتِجَدُوْنَ مُثْلَةْ لَمْ آمُرْبِهَا وَلَمْ تَسُوْنِيْ

96
00:06:58,776 --> 00:07:05,870
He said: Days rotate one day you win, and one day you lose

97
00:07:06,556 --> 00:07:10,571
and this day is our payback for the day of Badr(بدر).

98
00:07:13,644 --> 00:07:17,769
Meaning you won in Badr(بدر), we won this day.

99
00:07:18,559 --> 00:07:19,355
And then he said,

100
00:07:19,379 --> 00:07:23,979
وَسَتِجَدُوْنَ مُثْلَةْ لَمْ آمُرْبِهَا وَلَمْ تَسُوْنِيْ

101
00:07:24,378 --> 00:07:32,164
And you are going to find some mutilation, I did not order it but I also don’t disapprove it.

102
00:07:33,896 --> 00:07:42,319
He was referring to the bodies of the Muslims, who were mutilated such as body of Hamza Ibn Muttalib رضي الله عنه,

103
00:07:42,788 --> 00:07:43,981
his body was mutilated.

104
00:07:44,023 --> 00:07:48,195
Hind(هند) asked, for his liver to be plucked out, so that she can eat it.

105
00:07:49,024 --> 00:07:52,494
She had a bite from it, but then she spit it out.

106
00:07:53,949 --> 00:07:59,365
So, Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) is saying; I am not the one, who called for this mutilation of the bodies

107
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:03,066
 but in at the same time, I am not very upset about it, that it happened.

108
00:08:08,627 --> 00:08:09,690
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

109
00:08:09,725 --> 00:08:10,545
أَلَا تُجِيْبُوْا؟

110
00:08:10,604 --> 00:08:11,971
Aren’t you, going to respond back?

111
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:14,352
They said: What should we say?

112
00:08:14,593 --> 00:08:17,865
لَا سَوَاء قَتْلَانَا فِي الْجَنَّةْ وَ قَتْلَاكُمْ  فِى النَّارَ

113
00:08:17,883 --> 00:08:21,384
Respond back by saying; But we are not equal,

114
00:08:22,351 --> 00:08:25,818
our dead are in Paradise, and your dead are in Hell Fire.

115
00:08:26,262 --> 00:08:29,193
Because Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) was saying, that now its tit for tat, we are even.

116
00:08:29,463 --> 00:08:32,158
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying: No! We are not even it's not the same

117
00:08:32,550 --> 00:08:36,328
because dead among us, go to Jannah(جنة) and dead among you go to hellfire.

118
00:08:39,783 --> 00:08:42,122
It was Umar(عُمَر), who was doing the talking,

119
00:08:42,195 --> 00:08:47,013
 so Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) got bit closer to Umar(عُمَر) and he said:

120
00:08:49,039 --> 00:08:53,019
أُنْشِدُكَ الله ياعمر أَقَتَلْنَا محمد

121
00:08:53,154 --> 00:08:56,106
I ask you in the name of Allah, Umar(عُمَر) did we kill Muhammad(محمد)?

122
00:08:56,759 --> 00:08:57,976
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

123
00:08:58,230 --> 00:09:01,430
اَللَّهُمَّ لَا وَإِنَّه’ لَيَسْمَعُ كَلَامَكَ اَلْآنْ

124
00:09:02,315 --> 00:09:06,581
In the name of Allah! No! And he is right now, listening to you talking.

125
00:09:07,266 --> 00:09:08,471
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) said:

126
00:09:08,772 --> 00:09:13,872
 اَنْتَ اَصْدَقَ عِنْدِيْ وَأَبَرْ، اَنْتَ اَصْدَقْ عِنْدِيْ مِنْ اِبْنِ أَبِىْ قَمِئَةَ وَاَبَرْ

127
00:09:14,461 --> 00:09:19,585
You are more truthful to me, and righteous than Ibn Abi Qamia’h(ابن ابي قميه).

128
00:09:20,145 --> 00:09:22,994
I would believe you and not believe Ibn Abi Qamia’h(ابن ابي قميه).

129
00:09:29,205 --> 00:09:32,088
In the battle of Ghazwat Bani Al-Mutalaq(غزوة بني اَلْمُصْطَلَقْ),

130
00:09:36,185 --> 00:09:39,961
one of the Muhajireen(مهاجرين), he kicked one of the Ansaar(أنْصَار),

131
00:09:42,619 --> 00:09:43,901
so the Ansaari(أنْصَاري) said:

132
00:09:44,193 --> 00:09:45,473
يا لِلْاَ نْصَار

133
00:09:46,788 --> 00:09:52,333
He is calling the Ansaar(أنْصَار), to gang up on the Muhajiri(مهاجري)

134
00:09:53,359 --> 00:09:54,667
and the Muhajiri(مهاجري) said:

135
00:09:54,770 --> 00:09:56,070
 يا لِلْمُهَاجِرِيْن

136
00:09:56,845 --> 00:09:59,199
He is now calling for the Muhajireen(مهاجرين).

137
00:09:59,982 --> 00:10:07,467
And a fight was about to start between the Companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ for such a small affair.

138
00:10:08,847 --> 00:10:10,310
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

139
00:10:13,143 --> 00:10:17,082
اَبِدَعْوَى الْجَاهِلِيَّةْ وَأَنَا بَيْنَ أَظْهُرِكُمْ

140
00:10:17,346 --> 00:10:22,922
Are you calling to the slogans of Jahiliyah(جاهليه) and I am still living among you?

141
00:10:23,823 --> 00:10:28,387
You are calling for this Nationalism, this Tribalism, while I am still here?

142
00:10:29,317 --> 00:10:29,840
And then he said:

143
00:10:29,871 --> 00:10:31,347
دَعُوْهَا فَإِنَّهَا نَتِنَهْ

144
00:10:31,666 --> 00:10:34,088
Stay away from it, because it has evil smell.

145
00:10:35,048 --> 00:10:39,722
Rasool Allah ﷺ is talking about, the perils, the evils of nationalism and tribalism.

146
00:10:40,659 --> 00:10:44,782
He is telling them, to stay away from it, because it has an evil smell.

147
00:10:47,329 --> 00:10:51,388
Now, Abdullah Ibn Ubae(عبدالله إبن أبي), who was the head of the Munafiqeen(منافقين).

148
00:10:52,558 --> 00:10:55,968
When he heard about this incidence, he said:

149
00:10:57,141 --> 00:11:04,181
أَفَعَلُوْهَاأَمَا وَالله لَئِنْ رَجَعْنَا اِلَى الْمَدِيْنَةِ لَيُخْرِجَنَّ الأَعَزَّ مِنْهَا الّأَذَلْ

150
00:11:04,712 --> 00:11:05,890
That’s what they have done,

151
00:11:06,474 --> 00:11:12,113
when we go back to Madina, the noble one, will drive out the lowly one.

152
00:11:13,539 --> 00:11:17,158
What Abdullah Ibn Ubae(عبدالله إبن أبي) was referring to, is that.

153
00:11:17,558 --> 00:11:24,090
He, the noble one, is gonna drive out Muhammadﷺ, the lowly one.

154
00:11:25,617 --> 00:11:27,746
These were the words of the head of the Munafiqeen(منافقين).

155
00:11:31,579 --> 00:11:34,939
His son Abdullah(عبدالله) heard about this statements of his father.

156
00:11:38,867 --> 00:11:46,873
He stood on the entrance to Madina and he said to his father,

157
00:11:47,389 --> 00:11:49,958
I am not going to allow you in, he is holding his sword in his hand,

158
00:11:50,029 --> 00:11:54,236
he said: I am not gonna allow you in, until Rasool Allah ﷺ allows you in.

159
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:59,226
That shows you the loyalty that Islam has built

160
00:11:59,377 --> 00:12:03,156
 that he was willing to kill his father.

161
00:12:05,687 --> 00:12:08,467
If Rasool Allah ﷺ does not give him permission to come in.

162
00:12:09,587 --> 00:12:11,581
Now Umar Ibn Al-Khattabرضي الله عنه said:

163
00:12:12,437 --> 00:12:14,544
دَاعْنِيْ أَضْرِبْ عُنُقَ هَذَا الْمُنَافِقْ

164
00:12:14,841 --> 00:12:18,037
O Rasool Ullah, let me behead this Munafiq(منافق).

165
00:12:19,278 --> 00:12:20,951
What did Rasool Allah ﷺ say?

166
00:12:21,455 --> 00:12:22,328
 He said:

167
00:12:23,291 --> 00:12:28,359
لَا يَتَّحَدَّثُ النَّاس، اَنَّ محمدًا يَقْتُلُ اَصْحَابَهْ

168
00:12:29,330 --> 00:12:34,781
I don’t want people to say that Muhammad(محمد) is killing his followers.

169
00:12:36,917 --> 00:12:42,839
Over here Rasool Allah ﷺ is not disputing the fact, that Abdullah Ibn Ubae(عبدالله إبن أبي) deserves to die, for what he said,

170
00:12:43,766 --> 00:12:45,297
that was Kuffr(كفر), it was Riddah(ردة).

171
00:12:46,115 --> 00:12:51,440
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is not disputing the fact, that he deserved to be executed.

172
00:12:51,538 --> 00:12:58,800
 Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying the reason, why I am not going to implement that punishment against Abdullah Ibn Ubae(عبدالله إبن أبي),

173
00:12:59,130 --> 00:13:03,214
is because I don’t want people to say that Muhammad(محمد) is killing his followers.

174
00:13:04,224 --> 00:13:11,365
Rasool Allah ﷺ was concerned about the reputation of the Muslims.

175
00:13:11,706 --> 00:13:19,320
 Rasool Allah ﷺ has given a reputation of strength and unity, he has given reputation of loyalty

176
00:13:19,886 --> 00:13:26,381
 that the Muslims stick together that, they do not allow any of the enemy to come between them.

177
00:13:26,971 --> 00:13:35,502
And this has been witnessed by visitors who come to Madina from among the ranks, of the disbelievers.

178
00:13:36,017 --> 00:13:37,405
For example one of them said:

179
00:13:38,529 --> 00:13:43,170
I've visited the Roman Emperor in his palace,

180
00:13:43,749 --> 00:13:46,384
I've visited Persian Emperor in his palace,

181
00:13:46,582 --> 00:13:50,306
I've visited An-Najashi(النجاشي) in his palace,

182
00:13:51,151 --> 00:13:54,012
and I have seen how these kings and emperors were treated

183
00:13:54,836 --> 00:14:02,050
but I am telling you that, I have never, ever seen a people who respect and love their leader

184
00:14:02,653 --> 00:14:05,463
like the Sahabah(صحابه) love Muhammadﷺ.

185
00:14:06,616 --> 00:14:12,253
He would be making Wudu(وضؤ) and they would be jumping to grab the droplets of water, falling of his body

186
00:14:14,123 --> 00:14:15,964
and then, they would rub their bodies with it.

187
00:14:22,179 --> 00:14:26,523
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want the people to say, that Muhammadﷺ is killing his followers

188
00:14:27,288 --> 00:14:29,364
because that would turn people away from Islam.

189
00:14:30,723 --> 00:14:32,327
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying

190
00:14:32,504 --> 00:14:36,253
لَا يَتَّحَدَّثُ النَّاس، اَنَّ محمدًا يَقْتُلُ اَصْحَابَهْ

191
00:14:36,760 --> 00:14:39,912
I don’t want people to say that Muhammad(محمد) is killing his followers.

192
00:14:41,212 --> 00:14:42,995
Some lessons here,  N0: 1

193
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:45,639
The perils of nationalism,

194
00:14:45,667 --> 00:14:50,587
this is a disease which Rasool Allah ﷺ said, will carry on in my Ummah(امة).

195
00:14:51,450 --> 00:14:55,781
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Two things of Jahiliyah(جاهليه) will remain in you,

196
00:14:56,783 --> 00:14:59,759
this Asabiyyah(عصبية), this nationalism or tribalism

197
00:15:01,218 --> 00:15:03,797
and Niyahaa(نِيَاحَةْ) on the Mo'ta(مَوْتَى) the wailing on the dead.

198
00:15:05,593 --> 00:15:10,774
This is very dangerous disease and it's one of most important gateways of Shaytan(شيطان).

199
00:15:12,570 --> 00:15:14,188
So, Allahعزُّوَجل is warning us,

200
00:15:14,239 --> 00:15:18,936
وَقُلْ لِعِبَادِي يَقُولُوا الَّتِي هِيَ أَحْسَنُ ۚ إِنَّ الشَّيْطَانَ يَنْزَغُ بَيْنَهُمْ ۚ

201
00:15:20,207 --> 00:15:27,797
Tell My servants to speak good words because Shaytan(شيطان) causes disunity or rifts between them.

202
00:15:28,716 --> 00:15:34,875
You could say one word that would be misinterpreted by your brother and that could cause a war.

203
00:15:36,289 --> 00:15:41,679
All what Shaytan(شيطان) needs is you to make a slip of a tongue or a wrong word

204
00:15:42,087 --> 00:15:49,087
and then he plays in the heart of your brother by giving him a feeling of bad suspicion in what you have said

205
00:15:49,627 --> 00:15:52,468
 and after this he just picks up from there and flares up.

206
00:15:55,012 --> 00:15:59,536
All what cause this problem was for one of the Al-Muhajireen(المهاجرين) to kick one of the Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

207
00:15:59,573 --> 00:16:03,208
Allah-Ho-Alam( الله اعلم) if it was accidental or it was intended, Allah-Ho-Alam( الله اعلم).

208
00:16:03,599 --> 00:16:08,184
Anyway that was the reason, why they were about to fight each other.

209
00:16:09,624 --> 00:16:10,489
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying;

210
00:16:10,575 --> 00:16:12,689
اَبِدَعْوَى الْجَاهِلِيَّةْ وَأَنَا بَيْنَ أَظْهُرِكُمْ

211
00:16:13,765 --> 00:16:15,441
this is the call to Jahiliyyah(جاهليه).

212
00:16:16,948 --> 00:16:19,836
And this disease still exist among the Ummah(امة) today.

213
00:16:20,165 --> 00:16:22,284
There is racism, there is discrimination

214
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:29,843
you would rarely find any two neighbouring Muslim countries who don’t have bickering between them.

215
00:16:31,050 --> 00:16:34,534
They don’t have to be neighbouring, Pakistan and Bangladesh are not neighbouring.

216
00:16:37,222 --> 00:16:38,939
So, it's all over the Muslim world.

217
00:16:40,079 --> 00:16:46,833
Look at the Middle East, every country has problems with every country that is adjacent to it, that's bordering it.

218
00:16:48,271 --> 00:16:50,723
And then within the country you have different tribes

219
00:16:51,519 --> 00:16:53,209
and then within tribes, you've different clans

220
00:16:54,637 --> 00:16:56,244
that’s all Asabiyyah(عصبية) of Jahiliyyah(جاهليه).

221
00:16:56,291 --> 00:17:02,720
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: That belongs to the time of Ignorance, pre-Islamic Ignorance.

222
00:17:03,636 --> 00:17:04,863
So, we need to stay away from it.

223
00:17:07,892 --> 00:17:16,692
Everybody is equal and Allahعزُّوَجل differentiates between you, in your status according to your Taqwa(تقوى),

224
00:17:18,943 --> 00:17:20,909
إِنَّ أَكْرَمَكُمْ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ أَتْقَاكُمْ ۚ

225
00:17:22,447 --> 00:17:25,890
The closest to Allahعزُّوَجل among you are the ones, who have Taqwa(تقوى).

226
00:17:33,444 --> 00:17:34,429
IN SULHA-AL-HUDAYBIYYAH(صلح الحديبية)

227
00:17:40,250 --> 00:17:43,417
Umrah-Tul-Qadha(عمرة القضاء) and Sulha-Al-Hudaybiyya(صلح حديبة) we will talk about them together,

228
00:17:44,866 --> 00:17:49,906
Rasool Allah ﷺ went with Sahabah رضي الله عنهم with the intention of making Umrah(عمرة)

229
00:17:55,274 --> 00:17:59,178
but people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) prevented them from entering into Makkah.

230
00:18:01,372 --> 00:18:07,729
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to send one of his Sahabah(صحابه) to negotiate with the leaders of Makkah.

231
00:18:07,807 --> 00:18:16,371
So he proposed to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه that, he should go and negotiate with the people of Makkah.

232
00:18:17,086 --> 00:18:18,204
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

233
00:18:18,315 --> 00:18:26,233
O Messenger of Allah there is nobody of Bannu Udae(بنو عُدَي) in Makkah who, I can count on to give me protection.

234
00:18:26,854 --> 00:18:30,473
His clan, the clan of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was small

235
00:18:31,075 --> 00:18:36,557
and there wasn’t anybody in there, who was strong at the moment to offer Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) with protection.

236
00:18:36,649 --> 00:18:42,131
That was the system in those days every clan offer protection to his followers.

237
00:18:42,413 --> 00:18:45,298
If the clan is weak or small then you don’t get their protection.

238
00:18:46,221 --> 00:18:49,524
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Why don’t you tell Uthman(عثمان) to go,

239
00:18:49,920 --> 00:18:53,409
because his family can offer him with protection, Bannu Ummayah(بنوامية).

240
00:18:54,378 --> 00:18:57,175
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ agrees with the suggestion of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)

241
00:18:57,208 --> 00:19:00,981
and he sent Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) to go into Makkah.

242
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:06,976
Anyways, things developed from there, they were not allowed to go in

243
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:12,607
and they ended up signing up an agreement called Sulha-Al-Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبه),

244
00:19:13,079 --> 00:19:15,675
 the Peace Pact of Al-Hudaybiyyah(الحديبه).

245
00:19:17,292 --> 00:19:20,456
The terms in there, were not appealing to the Muslims

246
00:19:21,523 --> 00:19:24,127
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wasn't happy at all.

247
00:19:25,989 --> 00:19:28,431
Some of the terms in that Agreement.

248
00:19:28,812 --> 00:19:32,460
Number one, You don’t make Umrah(عمرة) and you go back.

249
00:19:34,144 --> 00:19:36,066
And they all came with the intention of Umrah(عمرة).

250
00:19:36,602 --> 00:19:37,277
Number two,

251
00:19:39,121 --> 00:19:45,566
If a Muslim comes from Makkah to Madina, after the signing of the Agreement he is turned away.

252
00:19:47,719 --> 00:19:52,775
But if a Muslim Apostates and leave from Madina to Makkah he is not turned away.

253
00:19:54,267 --> 00:19:55,953
So, this seems to be a double standard here.

254
00:19:56,496 --> 00:20:01,111
We turn away our people but you don’t turn away the people, who leave from among us.

255
00:20:03,369 --> 00:20:07,348
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and argued with him.

256
00:20:07,888 --> 00:20:08,526
 He said:

257
00:20:09,691 --> 00:20:10,952
أَلَسْتَ بِرَسُوْلِ الله؟

258
00:20:11,266 --> 00:20:12,769
Aren’t you the Messenger of Allah?

259
00:20:12,904 --> 00:20:14,808
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Balaa(بَلَى) Yes,

260
00:20:15,706 --> 00:20:17,077
أَلَسْنَا بِالْمُسْلِمِيْن؟

261
00:20:17,356 --> 00:20:18,661
Aren’t we the Muslims?

262
00:20:19,168 --> 00:20:20,790
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes!

263
00:20:21,192 --> 00:20:22,786
أَلَيْسُوْا بِالْمُشْرِكِيْنَ؟

264
00:20:23,092 --> 00:20:27,061
Aren’t these the Mushrikeen(مشركين), the disbelievers

265
00:20:27,387 --> 00:20:28,936
 Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes!

266
00:20:29,538 --> 00:20:30,458
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

267
00:20:30,510 --> 00:20:32,574
فَعَلَامَ نُعْطِي الدَّنِيَّةَ فِيْ دِيْنِنَا

268
00:20:33,152 --> 00:20:35,555
Why should we then agree to this compromise.?

269
00:20:36,746 --> 00:20:39,580
Why should we agree to these terms.?

270
00:20:40,461 --> 00:20:42,788
Rasool Allah ﷺ responded by saying:

271
00:20:42,900 --> 00:20:46,829
إِنِّيْ رَسُوْلُ الله وَلَسْتُ أَعْصِيْهِ وَهُوَ نَاصِرِيْ

272
00:20:48,125 --> 00:20:54,744
I am the Messenger of Allah and I am not going to disobey the commands of Allah and Allah will give me victory.

273
00:20:57,216 --> 00:21:01,464
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wasn’t satisfied, he went to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر).

274
00:21:02,424 --> 00:21:04,166
Umar(عمر) now went to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and told him.

275
00:21:04,713 --> 00:21:06,496
أَلَيْسَ بِرَسُوْلِ الله؟

276
00:21:07,148 --> 00:21:09,712
Isn’t he the Messenger of Allah? Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said: Yes!

277
00:21:10,349 --> 00:21:11,440
أَلَسْنَ بِالْمُسْلِمِيْن؟

278
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:12,585
Aren’t we the Muslims?

279
00:21:12,625 --> 00:21:13,748
 Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said: Yes,

280
00:21:14,401 --> 00:21:15,542
أَلَيْسُوْا بِالْمُشْرِكِيْنَ؟

281
00:21:15,593 --> 00:21:16,883
Aren’t these the disbelievers?

282
00:21:16,916 --> 00:21:18,018
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said: Yes,

283
00:21:18,314 --> 00:21:18,796
Umar(عُمَر) said:

284
00:21:18,825 --> 00:21:20,522
 "فَعَلَامَ نُعْطِي الدَّنِيَّةَ فِيْ دِيْنِنَا"

285
00:21:20,646 --> 00:21:23,328
Why should we then agree to such an Agreement.

286
00:21:25,053 --> 00:21:27,026
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

287
00:21:29,141 --> 00:21:41,319
اِلْزَمْ غَرْزَہ فَإِنِيْ أَشْهَدُ أَنَه، رَسُوْلُ الله وَأَنَّ الْحَقَ مَا اَمَرَبِهِ وَلَنْ نُخَالِفَ اَمَرَ الله وَلَنْ يُضَيِّعَهُ الله

288
00:21:42,044 --> 00:21:43,164
(اِلْزَمْ غَرْزَةْ)

289
00:21:43,255 --> 00:21:44,391
stick to his stirrups,

290
00:21:44,531 --> 00:21:47,165
the stirrups of where you put your feet in when you are riding the horse.

291
00:21:47,534 --> 00:21:52,782
Stick to them, meaning stick to whatever he does, don’t move an inch

292
00:21:53,178 --> 00:21:59,290
from the way of Rasool Allah ﷺ because I witnessed that he is Messenger of Allah

293
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:04,744
and that what Allah tells him is the truth and that Allahعَزّ وَجَلّ will not forsake His Messenger.

294
00:22:06,117 --> 00:22:09,395
That was the Yaqeen(يقين) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

295
00:22:09,671 --> 00:22:14,404
Yes, may be these terms doesn’t make any sense to us however, what he does is right.

296
00:22:14,989 --> 00:22:18,621
And if it's a command of Allahعَزّ وجَلّ then it's right and true

297
00:22:18,825 --> 00:22:22,589
 and Allahعَزّ وجَلّ has promised to give His Prophet victory He will give it to him.

298
00:22:23,864 --> 00:22:26,631
One of the concerns that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had, is about Umrah(عمرة)

299
00:22:27,330 --> 00:22:31,046
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) told Rasool Allah ﷺ in the earlier conversation.

300
00:22:32,213 --> 00:22:34,443
Didn’t you promise us that we will make an Umrah(عمرة)?

301
00:22:35,509 --> 00:22:37,240
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Yes, I did,

302
00:22:37,591 --> 00:22:40,439
But did I promise you that you will make it this year.

303
00:22:42,011 --> 00:22:42,717
Umar(عُمَر) said: No,

304
00:22:42,757 --> 00:22:46,568
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Then you will make Umrah(عمرة), you will make Tawaf(طواف) around the house of Allah.

305
00:22:50,289 --> 00:22:56,502
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), it was his zeal, that drove him into this conversation.

306
00:22:58,565 --> 00:23:01,367
But after he heard the response of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر)

307
00:23:03,051 --> 00:23:08,019
you know at times of difficulty the Sahabah(صحابه) would go to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر),

308
00:23:08,101 --> 00:23:10,027
 Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was the Sheikh(شيخ) of Sahabah(صحابه)

309
00:23:11,434 --> 00:23:18,101
and his response would put an end to their arguments, and would give them tranquility in their hearts.

310
00:23:18,997 --> 00:23:20,721
It happened when Rasool Allah ﷺ died,

311
00:23:21,289 --> 00:23:24,138
it happened when they disputed on the Khilafah(خِلَافَه),

312
00:23:24,704 --> 00:23:27,613
it happened on the issue of Army of Usamah(اسامه),

313
00:23:27,762 --> 00:23:31,038
it happened on the appointment of Usamah(اسامه) as the leader of the Army.

314
00:23:31,366 --> 00:23:36,541
Every time it was Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه, who would give them peace.

315
00:23:38,575 --> 00:23:42,925
When Umar(عُمَر) heard the response of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) he felt that he has done something wrong,

316
00:23:43,357 --> 00:23:47,700
he shouldn’t have argued with Rasool Allah ﷺ back and forth.

317
00:23:48,633 --> 00:23:49,902
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) says;

318
00:23:50,370 --> 00:23:54,263
مَا زِلْتُ أَتَصَدَّقْ وَأَصُوْم وَ أَعْتِقْ وَاُصَلِّى

319
00:23:54,571 --> 00:23:58,627
مِنَّ الَّذِيْ صَنَعْتُ يَوْمَئِذٍ مَخَافَةْ كَلَامِى الَّذِيْ تَكَلَّمْتُ بِهْ

320
00:24:00,330 --> 00:24:06,159
After that I would give Sadaqah(صدقه) I would fast I would free slaves and I would pray

321
00:24:07,341 --> 00:24:10,029
because of the words that I have spoken on that day.

322
00:24:11,846 --> 00:24:15,039
And this is very important lesson for us, when you commit a sin

323
00:24:16,717 --> 00:24:21,289
if you want to wipe out that sin, what you do is, do good deeds.

324
00:24:22,362 --> 00:24:24,751
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) felt that he has commited a mistake

325
00:24:25,319 --> 00:24:29,978
therefore, he was fasting, praying , freeing slaves, giving Sadaqah(صدقه)

326
00:24:30,762 --> 00:24:35,837
not just once of each, he was doing it more than once.

327
00:24:37,219 --> 00:24:39,552
So, that Allahعَزّ وجَلّ will forgive him for what he did.

328
00:24:39,727 --> 00:24:40,893
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ says;

329
00:24:41,131 --> 00:24:43,823
إِنَّ الْحَسَنَاتِ يُذْهِبْنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ ۚ

330
00:24:44,893 --> 00:24:48,134
Good deeds wipes out the evil deeds.

331
00:24:49,722 --> 00:24:54,831
So, to wash away your sins, to cleanse your body, do good deeds.

332
00:25:01,723 --> 00:25:07,183
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه he says, he had a statement but briefly he said:

333
00:25:10,814 --> 00:25:12,726
People have short vision

334
00:25:15,254 --> 00:25:19,754
and they fail to see that Allahعَزّ وجَلّ has a plan

335
00:25:22,329 --> 00:25:24,865
and that plan takes its time.

336
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:28,499
He was talking about Sulha-Al-Hudaybiyyah(صلح الحديبه).

337
00:25:32,050 --> 00:25:37,424
He said: They failed to see the wisdom behind this Sulha(صلح).

338
00:25:40,029 --> 00:25:46,007
He said: A short while later, I saw Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو),

339
00:25:46,159 --> 00:25:53,819
Suhail Ibn Amr (سهيل ابن عمرو) was the one who represented the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) in signing the Agreement with Rasool Allah ﷺ.

340
00:25:54,485 --> 00:25:56,414
And he was very argumentative, for example,

341
00:25:56,454 --> 00:26:02,572
when Rasool Allah ﷺ was dictating to Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) what to write.

342
00:26:02,783 --> 00:26:04,242
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, write

343
00:26:04,384 --> 00:26:05,984
 بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم

344
00:26:07,322 --> 00:26:07,974
so, Ali(علي) wrote

345
00:26:07,998 --> 00:26:09,081
 بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم

346
00:26:09,105 --> 00:26:11,422
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو) said: No, We don’t know Ar-Rahman(الرحمن) Ar-Raheem(الرحيم)

347
00:26:12,329 --> 00:26:16,203
write; Bismekallah Hum(بسمك اللهم), In the name of God, you have to be neutral.

348
00:26:18,123 --> 00:26:19,234
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

349
00:26:19,299 --> 00:26:22,561
 هَذَا مَا صَالِحَ عَلَيْهِ محمد رسول الله

350
00:26:22,644 --> 00:26:25,294
This is an agreement between Muhammad Rasool Ullah,

351
00:26:25,490 --> 00:26:27,410
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو) interrupts and says: No!

352
00:26:27,830 --> 00:26:32,787
If we agree that you are Messenger of Allah, we wouldn’t be negotiating with you to start with,

353
00:26:33,619 --> 00:26:36,069
but write your name and your father.

354
00:26:36,675 --> 00:26:37,789
Muhammad Ibn Abdullah(محمد ابن عبدالله)

355
00:26:39,170 --> 00:26:41,646
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ali(علي) wipe it out, erase it.

356
00:26:42,035 --> 00:26:43,696
Ali(علي) didn’t want to erase it,

357
00:26:44,054 --> 00:26:46,109
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ali(علي) show me, where it is.

358
00:26:46,387 --> 00:26:48,978
Rasool Allah ﷺ was illiterate, show me where it is.

359
00:26:49,505 --> 00:26:52,665
So, Ali(علي) pointed to it, Rasool Allah ﷺ erased it, with his own hand.

360
00:26:54,600 --> 00:26:59,719
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو), who was representing the Kuffar(كفار) in this Agreement.

361
00:27:00,260 --> 00:27:02,460
A year later Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) said:

362
00:27:02,531 --> 00:27:09,303
I saw him with my own eyes bringing the camels to Rasool Allah ﷺ after his Umrah(عمرة),

363
00:27:10,354 --> 00:27:12,402
for Rasool Allah ﷺ to sacrifice them.

364
00:27:13,757 --> 00:27:21,676
And then I saw when the barber of Rasool Allah ﷺ was shaving his head

365
00:27:23,327 --> 00:27:30,394
I saw Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو) going down on his knees and picking the clipping of Rasool Allah ﷺ

366
00:27:30,980 --> 00:27:34,178
and putting them on his eyes, to get Barakah(بركة) from him.

367
00:27:35,975 --> 00:27:38,494
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) is saying, people have a short vision

368
00:27:40,787 --> 00:27:44,668
this was a short while later, look at how the hearts changed.

369
00:27:45,393 --> 00:27:47,111
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل ابن عمرو) was now a Muslim.

370
00:27:48,585 --> 00:27:52,355
Islam spread like a wild fire when there was peace.

371
00:28:01,986 --> 00:28:03,202
Before Fateh Makkah(فتح المكة)

372
00:28:08,962 --> 00:28:20,624
Rasool Allah ﷺ was preparing his army but he made his destination secret.

373
00:28:22,342 --> 00:28:27,277
Rasool Allah ﷺ didn’t want to give the people of Makkah time to prepare to fight.

374
00:28:27,990 --> 00:28:28,391
Why?

375
00:28:28,431 --> 00:28:31,565
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ didn’t want to cause bloodshed in Makkah.

376
00:28:32,748 --> 00:28:41,034
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to ambush them within over whelming force, so that they give up and don’t fight.

377
00:28:42,037 --> 00:28:47,078
So, he didn’t want anyone to know that he is going to Makkah, so that the people of Makkah wouldn’t prepare.

378
00:28:47,442 --> 00:28:50,573
He knew their nature, they are stubborn, they are gonna try to fight.

379
00:28:51,497 --> 00:28:57,366
So, he wanted to make sure that he assembles a large army overwhelming force not to give them even a chance.

380
00:29:00,285 --> 00:29:03,180
However, one of the Sahabah(صحابه), Haatib Ibn Abi Balta’ah(حاطب ابن ابى بلتعة)

381
00:29:04,679 --> 00:29:13,335
he writes a letter, to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), telling them, that Muhammad(محمد) plans to attack you.

382
00:29:14,795 --> 00:29:19,787
And he sends it with a woman, who is traveling to Makkah and he pays her.

383
00:29:23,634 --> 00:29:25,851
Rasool Allah ﷺ receives revelation.

384
00:29:27,016 --> 00:29:31,714
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) comes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and tells him about what happened.

385
00:29:32,669 --> 00:29:41,163
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ sends Ali(علي), Al-Miqdad(المقداد) and Az-Zubair(الزبير) to pursue this woman.

386
00:29:42,552 --> 00:29:45,982
So, they go to a place called Rawdhat Khakh(روضة الخاخ)

387
00:29:47,463 --> 00:29:52,647
and they approached the woman and they tell her, give us the message that you have.

388
00:29:52,986 --> 00:29:54,314
 She said: I don’t have anything.

389
00:29:55,032 --> 00:29:59,500
They said: Either you hand it over to us otherwise we are gonna take off your clothes.

390
00:30:01,432 --> 00:30:08,341
And this shows you that you could rough up, a person in interrogation, to certain extent.

391
00:30:09,434 --> 00:30:14,864
And exposing the Awrah(عورة), is allowed in such situations.

392
00:30:14,911 --> 00:30:16,948
 They threatened her that they are going to take off her clothes.

393
00:30:17,382 --> 00:30:18,332
Hand us over the message!

394
00:30:19,713 --> 00:30:27,591
When she saw that they are serious, she pulled it out from her braids.

395
00:30:30,176 --> 00:30:35,017
It was hidden very well and they carried the letter back to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

396
00:30:39,876 --> 00:30:43,776
Rasool Allah ﷺ calls in, Haatib(حاطب) and he tells him, why did you do that?

397
00:30:44,929 --> 00:30:46,814
Haatib(حاطب) he said:

398
00:30:46,872 --> 00:30:48,434
يا رسول الله لَا تَعْجَلْ عَلَيْ

399
00:30:48,487 --> 00:30:52,148
O Rasool Ullah! Don’t rush to Judgment about me.

400
00:30:53,723 --> 00:30:58,067
اِنِّيْ كُنْتُ اِمْرَأً مُلْصَقًا فِيْ قُرَيْشْ وَلَمْ أَكُنْ مِنْ أَنْفُسِهَا

401
00:30:59,329 --> 00:31:03,152
O Rasool Ullah I was a man didn’t belong to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

402
00:31:05,184 --> 00:31:10,582
وَكَانَ مَنْ مَّعَكَ مِنَّ الْمُهَاجِرِيْنَ مَنْ لَّهُمْ قَرَابَاتٍ يَحْمُوْنَ بِهَا اَهْلِهِمْ وَاَمْوَالَهُمْ

403
00:31:11,325 --> 00:31:17,460
While rest of the Muhajireen(مهاجرين), have families back in Makkah, who take care of their interest, their family, their wealth,

404
00:31:19,791 --> 00:31:26,313
فَاَحْبَبْتُ إِذَ فَاتَنِيْ ذَلِكَ مِنْ النَّسَبِ فِيْهِمْ أَنْ أَتَّخِذَ عِنْدَهُمْ يَدَا يَحْمُوْنَ قَرَابتيْ

405
00:31:28,407 --> 00:31:34,065
So, I wanted to do them a favor so that they would do me a favor and protect my family in Makkah.

406
00:31:36,425 --> 00:31:41,347
وَلَمْ أَفْعَلْ ذَالِكَ اِرْتِدَادًا عَنْ دِيْنِى وَلَا رِضًا بِكُفْرِبَعْدَ الْإِسْلَامْ

407
00:31:41,635 --> 00:31:44,754
I didn’t do that because I have apostated

408
00:31:45,013 --> 00:31:47,522
or because I prefer Kuffr(كفر) over Eeman(ايمان).

409
00:31:48,593 --> 00:31:50,680
So, Haatib(حاطب) is explaining why he did that.

410
00:31:51,564 --> 00:31:55,421
I didn’t do it, because I want to betray Allahعَزّ وجَلّ and His Messenger.

411
00:31:55,472 --> 00:31:58,670
 I didn’t do it, because I have apostated, because I loved Kuffr(كفر).

412
00:31:59,345 --> 00:32:03,396
I did it because, I was worried about safety of my family in Makkah.

413
00:32:04,221 --> 00:32:08,087
And since rest of the Companions have relatives to take care of their families,

414
00:32:08,535 --> 00:32:14,477
I wanted to do this for the Kuffar(كفار), so they would in exchange protect my family.

415
00:32:15,787 --> 00:32:16,981
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

416
00:32:17,944 --> 00:32:19,453
اَمَا اِنَّه’ قَدْ صَدَقَكُمْ

417
00:32:19,988 --> 00:32:21,507
He is telling us the truth.

418
00:32:22,053 --> 00:32:23,455
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

419
00:32:23,791 --> 00:32:26,889
يا رسول الله ،دَعْنِي أَضْرِبْ عُنُقَ هَذَا الْمُنَافِقْ

420
00:32:27,635 --> 00:32:30,778
O Rasool Ullah! Allow me to behead this Munafiq(منافق).

421
00:32:31,543 --> 00:32:34,234
He is a hypocrite, and he needs to be beheaded!

422
00:32:36,706 --> 00:32:38,507
Rasool Allah ﷺ said:

423
00:32:39,934 --> 00:32:41,745
إِنَّه’ قَدْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا

424
00:32:41,793 --> 00:32:46,601
وَمَا يَدْرِيْكَ لَعَلَّ الله إِطَّلَعَ عَلى مَنْ شَهِدَا بَدَرْ فَقَالْ

425
00:32:46,818 --> 00:32:49,490
 إعْمَلُوْا مَا شِـئْتُمْ فَقَدْ غَفَرْتُ لَكُمْ

426
00:32:51,587 --> 00:33:02,118
He has witnessed Badr(بدر) and you never know may be Allah has looked upon the people of Badr(بدر) and said:

427
00:33:02,490 --> 00:33:07,340
Do whatever you want, because I have forgiven you.

428
00:33:09,295 --> 00:33:14,315
You are forgiven, your sins are forgiven and this is in Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ).

429
00:33:16,887 --> 00:33:19,737
A FEW LESSONS TO LEARN FROM THIS HADITH(حديث):

430
00:33:19,777 --> 00:33:20,695
Number One,

431
00:33:21,287 --> 00:33:28,723
The Hukum(حكم), the Ruling regarding the SPY, the one who spies, against Muslims, is execution.

432
00:33:29,953 --> 00:33:34,495
That’s ruling regarding the one, who spies against the Muslims.

433
00:33:37,317 --> 00:33:41,714
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ didn’t dispute what Umar(عُمَر) said, when he said: He should be beheaded.

434
00:33:42,788 --> 00:33:45,269
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: It is because he witnessed Badr(بدر)

435
00:33:45,851 --> 00:33:50,771
and Allah has granted them forgiveness that’s why he shouldn’t be beheaded.

436
00:33:50,864 --> 00:33:53,541
If it was somebody else, he would be executed.

437
00:33:55,497 --> 00:34:04,112
So, this is a stern warning for those, who betray Allahعَزّ وجَلّ and His Messenger and spy against the Muslims.

438
00:34:06,373 --> 00:34:08,830
Their Hukum(حكم) is execution

439
00:34:09,121 --> 00:34:18,789
and if a person is doing it, and they are agreeing with what they are doing, they think that what they are doing is right,

440
00:34:19,805 --> 00:34:24,145
no matter who they are doing it for, that is Ridda(ردّة), that is Kuffr(كفر).

441
00:34:25,079 --> 00:34:28,443
And if they are doing it for a reason such as Haatib(حاطب), because of fear

442
00:34:28,785 --> 00:34:34,374
because of love of Duniyah(دُنِيَّا), love of money, then that is a major sin,

443
00:34:35,203 --> 00:34:36,736
but the punishment is still the same.

444
00:34:39,045 --> 00:34:48,854
So, this thing of working for the enemies of Allah in order to spy against the Muslims,

445
00:34:49,029 --> 00:34:55,218
no matter who this Muslim is, as long as they are still a Muslim, regardless of what they are doing.

446
00:34:55,519 --> 00:34:58,024
Even if what they are doing, is something you disagree with,

447
00:34:58,530 --> 00:35:02,526
even if what they are doing something that is against your methodology

448
00:35:02,606 --> 00:35:06,047
or the way or the movement of the ideology that you follow

449
00:35:06,483 --> 00:35:11,459
as long as they are Muslims, who testify that there is no god but Allah and Muhammad(محمد) is the Messenger of Allah

450
00:35:11,767 --> 00:35:16,616
spying against them is Ridda(ردّة) if you agree with, what you are doing.

451
00:35:16,950 --> 00:35:18,649
You have left the folds of Islam.

452
00:35:24,404 --> 00:35:26,404
The Second lesson,

453
00:35:27,924 --> 00:35:29,546
 this is a sin to be exposed,

454
00:35:30,133 --> 00:35:35,292
 we know that the sins of a Muslims should be concealed, they should not be made public.

455
00:35:36,540 --> 00:35:40,385
For example, A Muslim drinks and they don’t want anybody to know about it.

456
00:35:40,712 --> 00:35:43,361
Don’t go around, saying that this person drinks.

457
00:35:44,783 --> 00:35:50,981
If a brother is using drugs and they are ashamed of what they are doing

458
00:35:51,227 --> 00:35:54,992
 and they are doing it in a secret, they don’t want anybody to know, and you happen to know.

459
00:35:55,229 --> 00:35:57,662
 You don’t go around exposing that sin.

460
00:35:59,120 --> 00:36:03,517
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ loves the sins of a believers to be concealed, Sittr(ستر).

461
00:36:04,326 --> 00:36:08,524
Allah loves the sins to be concealed, not made public.

462
00:36:09,736 --> 00:36:14,244
However, with this particular sin it should be made public and exposed,

463
00:36:14,680 --> 00:36:16,873
 And we see if from the Hadith(حديث), it was exposed.

464
00:36:16,929 --> 00:36:19,328
Rasool Allah ﷺ brought Haatib(حاطب) in front of everyone.

465
00:36:20,780 --> 00:36:28,048
When we know in other occasions Rasool Allah will tell a person, for example in adultery, go back, don’t speak about this,

466
00:36:28,718 --> 00:36:32,877
or the man, who came and said: I was drinking, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him to leave.

467
00:36:36,075 --> 00:36:40,123
An-Nawwawi(النووي) says: Sins are only exposed if there is benefit in exposing them.

468
00:36:40,191 --> 00:36:44,350
 So this sin because it's against the community, it needs to be exposed

469
00:36:44,403 --> 00:36:48,661
 and people need to know that, this person has betrayed Allah and His Messenger.

470
00:36:57,428 --> 00:37:00,774
And Ya'ani(يعني) I hope that I have driven the point and made it very clear

471
00:37:00,943 --> 00:37:04,183
as long as the person is a Muslim no matter what they are doing,

472
00:37:04,658 --> 00:37:08,475
no matter what, you do not spy against them.

473
00:37:13,336 --> 00:37:15,367
Finally the third lesson,

474
00:37:17,308 --> 00:37:19,102
- the virtues of the people of Badr(بدر).

475
00:37:20,861 --> 00:37:25,956
These selected few, who have witnessed the Battle of Badr(بدر),

476
00:37:26,785 --> 00:37:29,762
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ has granted them forgiveness.

477
00:37:30,468 --> 00:37:38,094
Even though Haatib(حاطب) committed such a major sin Rasool Allah ﷺ lets him go, without punishment.

478
00:37:38,578 --> 00:37:39,161
 Why?

479
00:37:39,312 --> 00:37:40,939
Because he attended Badr(بدر).

480
00:37:41,807 --> 00:37:46,758
So, Allah granted them forgiveness that extends to the future.

481
00:37:47,789 --> 00:37:51,889
It's not just the past sins but it also extends to the future.

482
00:37:52,810 --> 00:37:55,961
It’s a Maghfirah(مغفرة) of the past and the future.

483
00:37:58,663 --> 00:38:03,876
The ones who attended Badr(بدر) are The Best of Muslims and Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) comes to Muhammadﷺ and says:

484
00:38:04,140 --> 00:38:08,130
The ones, who attended The Badr(بدر) from among the angels are also the Best of Angels.

485
00:38:08,834 --> 00:38:11,345
Its not just for the humans, it's also for the angels.

486
00:38:15,789 --> 00:38:20,281
When the army of Rasool Allah ﷺ came closer to Makkah.

487
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:26,946
Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) came to see the army.

488
00:38:32,598 --> 00:38:33,937
So Al-Abbas(العباس) told him:

489
00:38:35,715 --> 00:38:38,509
If you are seen like that, you are going to be killed.

490
00:38:40,258 --> 00:38:41,810
So Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) said: What should I do?

491
00:38:41,850 --> 00:38:44,191
Now Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) is lost, that’s it.

492
00:38:44,666 --> 00:38:46,893
Everything is gone, his leadership in Makkah is gone.

493
00:38:47,078 --> 00:38:52,496
Makkah will be conquered by the Muslims, Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) doesn’t know what to do.

494
00:38:53,814 --> 00:38:55,196
He is in state of loss.

495
00:38:55,806 --> 00:38:58,730
Al-Abbas(العباس), the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ told him:

496
00:38:59,779 --> 00:39:07,536
You ride with me on the Mount of Rasool Ullah, whether it was his camel or donkey

497
00:39:10,326 --> 00:39:14,151
and when people see you riding the donkey of Rasool Allah ﷺ they are going to leave you alone.

498
00:39:15,563 --> 00:39:22,087
So, he was riding and whenever he passed next to a camp fire of Muslims they will say who is it.

499
00:39:22,863 --> 00:39:28,625
But when they see the donkey of Rasool Allah ﷺ they let him go, without even asking who is on it.

500
00:39:28,665 --> 00:39:32,885
That’s it, it is the donkey of Rasool Ullah whoever is it, he is granted a free pass.

501
00:39:33,909 --> 00:39:36,479
Until they passed to the camp fire of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

502
00:39:39,155 --> 00:39:39,860
Umar(عُمَر) said:

503
00:39:39,895 --> 00:39:47,939
 عَدُوَّا الله قَدْ اَمْكَنَ الله مِنْكَ بِغَيْرِ عَهْدٍ وَلَا ذِ مَّةْ

504
00:39:49,339 --> 00:39:56,116
The Enemy of Allah! Allah has brought you to us and you don’t have any Agreement of Peace with us,

505
00:39:57,066 --> 00:39:59,321
in other words you are gonna be dead.

506
00:40:00,587 --> 00:40:02,661
So, he rushes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and says:

507
00:40:03,007 --> 00:40:08,594
O Messenger of Allah! The enemy of Allah is here and we don’t have any peace agreement with him,

508
00:40:09,642 --> 00:40:10,911
 so let's execute him.

509
00:40:12,838 --> 00:40:17,969
Al-Abbas(العباس) said: I am giving him protection O Messenger of Allah, I have granted him protection.

510
00:40:18,473 --> 00:40:24,935
 Umar(عُمَر) argued with Al-Abbas(العباس) and they went on arguing and then Al-Abbas(العباس) said:

511
00:40:25,288 --> 00:40:32,854
Slow down Umar(عُمَر) if he was one of Bannu Ada'e(بنو عدى) you wouldn’t have say, what you are saying.

512
00:40:34,346 --> 00:40:39,060
But just because he is from Bannu Abd Manaf(بنو عبد مناف) its not from your clan, you want him executed.

513
00:40:41,104 --> 00:40:44,265
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Slow down Al-Abbas(العباس)

514
00:40:46,896 --> 00:40:51,502
your Islam was more beloved to me, than if my father would have become a Muslim.

515
00:40:53,620 --> 00:41:01,775
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) does not make his decision based on relationship, based on his clan or his tribe.

516
00:41:03,008 --> 00:41:08,159
Umar(عُمَر) is saying that the Islam of Al-Abbas(العباس), the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ was dearer to him,

517
00:41:08,452 --> 00:41:10,498
then if his father would have became Muslim.

518
00:41:11,030 --> 00:41:14,361
His own father! He would rather have Al-Abbas(العباس) become a Muslim

519
00:41:14,533 --> 00:41:17,793
and then Umar(عُمَر) said: Because I know that that pleases Rasool Ullah.

520
00:41:18,933 --> 00:41:24,550
Because your Islam would be to please Rasool Allah ﷺ, I am happier that you have become Muslim, then if my father became Muslim.

521
00:41:28,584 --> 00:41:34,433
Because Al-Abbas(العباس) granted Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) protection, Rasool Allah ﷺ set him free.

522
00:41:36,761 --> 00:41:44,745
But you see that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had this clear understanding of Al-Wala Wal-Bara(الولاء والبراء)

523
00:41:44,956 --> 00:41:52,747
who he gives his loyalty to, and who he is against, he would not follow his emotions in that.

524
00:41:53,260 --> 00:42:00,243
He would go with what pleases Allahعَزّوجَلّ and pleases, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.

525
00:42:10,126 --> 00:42:12,839
UMAR IBN KHATTAB(عمرابن الخطاب) IN MADINA:

526
00:42:18,502 --> 00:42:24,597
In Sahih Al-Muslim(صحيح المسلم), Abu Hurairah رضي الله عنه said;

527
00:42:24,629 --> 00:42:32,181
We were sitting with Rasool Allah ﷺ among us were Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and Umar(عُمَر) and then Rasool Allah ﷺ left.

528
00:42:33,110 --> 00:42:39,915
And he didn’t come back, so we were afraid that, may be something happened to him.

529
00:42:40,805 --> 00:42:44,551
And this shows the deep concern that the Sahabah(صحابه) had for Rasool Allah ﷺ

530
00:42:44,591 --> 00:42:47,313
whenever he would be delayed or late they would worry.

531
00:42:49,592 --> 00:42:52,726
They loved him more than their wives, and their children and their parents.

532
00:42:53,692 --> 00:42:57,315
In fact the common terms they would use with Rasool Allah ﷺ,

533
00:42:57,960 --> 00:42:59,290
بِأبِيْ أنْتَ وَاُمِّي،ِأبِيْ أنْتَ وَاُمِّي

534
00:43:00,442 --> 00:43:01,454
بِأبِيْ أنْتَ وَاُمِّي،ِأبِيْ أنْتَ وَاُمِّي

535
00:43:01,490 --> 00:43:01,961
Means!

536
00:43:02,370 --> 00:43:05,008
I would sacrifice my father and my mother for you.

537
00:43:06,120 --> 00:43:09,630
That’s a statement, you always read that in the Hadith(حديث).

538
00:43:09,937 --> 00:43:11,471
بِأبِيْ أنْتَ وَاُمِّي يا رسول الله

539
00:43:13,858 --> 00:43:18,553
So, Abu Hurairah(ابوهرير) said: I was the first to go and look for him.

540
00:43:19,995 --> 00:43:25,130
So I came to this farm there was a wall surrounding it

541
00:43:26,021 --> 00:43:29,495
and I went around the farm and I didn’t find any entrance, any gate.

542
00:43:31,453 --> 00:43:39,204
But I saw a small crack in which water was flowing into or out of the farm.

543
00:43:39,806 --> 00:43:42,070
So, I squeezed myself in like a fox would.

544
00:43:42,838 --> 00:43:48,270
You know, you'd see a big fox and in a small hole, but still she is able to go through it.

545
00:43:48,738 --> 00:43:49,373
So, Abu Hurairah(ابوهرير) said:

546
00:43:49,397 --> 00:43:51,357
 فَإحْتَفَزْتُ كَمَا يَحْتَفَزَالثَّعْلَبْ

547
00:43:51,881 --> 00:43:54,689
I squeezed myself through like a fox would.

548
00:43:56,888 --> 00:43:58,701
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Aba Hurairah(اَبَا هريرة)

549
00:43:59,090 --> 00:44:00,956
Are you Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرۃ)? Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرۃ) said: Yes!

550
00:44:01,430 --> 00:44:03,233
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Ya Aba Hurairah(يا ابا هريره),

551
00:44:03,415 --> 00:44:09,453
O Abu Hurairah(اَبوهريرة): Take these sandals of mine, this shoes, take them

552
00:44:10,686 --> 00:44:15,096
and whomever you meet behind this wall, who says,

553
00:44:15,136 --> 00:44:16,638
 لا اله الا الله

554
00:44:17,025 --> 00:44:20,743
with Yaqeen(يقين) in their heart give them the glad tidings of the Jannah(جنة),

555
00:44:22,399 --> 00:44:28,705
مَلْ لَقِيْتَهْ يَشْهَدُ ألَّا الله إِلَّا الله مُسْتَيْقَنَا بِهَا قَلْبُهْ فَبَشِّرْه’ بِالْجَنَّةً

556
00:44:34,576 --> 00:44:38,391
Abu Hurairah(ابوهرير) took the sandals of Rasool Ullah.

557
00:44:38,735 --> 00:44:44,783
Now the sandals are symbolic or an evidence that he is carrying a message from Rasool Ullah,

558
00:44:44,998 --> 00:44:46,879
I have something from Rasool Allah with me.

559
00:44:49,107 --> 00:44:51,142
The first one he meets was Umar(عُمَر).

560
00:44:54,284 --> 00:44:58,425
He says: Rasool Allah sent me, with his sandals and told me

561
00:44:59,961 --> 00:45:08,457
to give the glad tidings to anyone I meet, who testifies that there is no god but Allah with Yaqeen(يقين) in their heart

562
00:45:09,651 --> 00:45:11,231
give them the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة).

563
00:45:13,052 --> 00:45:14,978
What do you expect the response of Umar(عُمَر) was?

564
00:45:17,185 --> 00:45:21,408
Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر) Al-Hamdolillah(الحمدلله), I am so happy go and tell the people about it.?

565
00:45:24,379 --> 00:45:25,983
It was a strange response.

566
00:45:27,475 --> 00:45:34,643
Umar(عُمَر) punches Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرۃ) in his chest until, Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرۃ) falls on his back.

567
00:45:35,374 --> 00:45:41,755
It was such a rough punch, Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرۃ) flew and fell on his back.

568
00:45:43,160 --> 00:45:47,083
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرۃ) said: I stood up and I went to Rasool Allah ﷺ crying,

569
00:45:48,250 --> 00:45:49,170
I was crying.

570
00:45:49,448 --> 00:45:54,583
 Now, obviously he had to cry nobody fights with Umar(عُمَر), you don’t fight with Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).

571
00:45:55,317 --> 00:45:57,231
You swallow, you swallow it,

572
00:45:59,687 --> 00:46:02,522
He goes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and he said: Umar(عُمَر) followed me.

573
00:46:06,363 --> 00:46:12,311
And he came in and he was crying, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: what happened Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرۃ)?

574
00:46:13,049 --> 00:46:17,008
Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرۃ) said: You sent me to give glad tidings to the people and I give him glad tidings,

575
00:46:17,269 --> 00:46:19,767
he punches me, until I fall on my back.

576
00:46:20,656 --> 00:46:22,577
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Umar(عُمَر): why did you do that?

577
00:46:23,426 --> 00:46:27,664
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرإبن الخطاب) said: Did you tell him to go and give glad tidings to the people,

578
00:46:27,854 --> 00:46:29,341
that they are granted Jannah(جنة) if they say,

579
00:46:29,388 --> 00:46:30,505
اشهد ان لا اله الا الله

580
00:46:30,545 --> 00:46:31,165
with Yaqeen(يقين).

581
00:46:31,428 --> 00:46:32,782
Rasool Allah ﷺ says: Yes

582
00:46:32,855 --> 00:46:41,138
Umar(عُمَر) said: Don’t do that, because people will take that for granted,

583
00:46:42,309 --> 00:46:46,214
so let them work for it.

584
00:46:46,888 --> 00:46:49,547
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Then we will let them work for it.

585
00:46:50,654 --> 00:46:52,986
Rasool Allah ﷺ would go with the opinion of Umar(عُمَر).

586
00:46:54,243 --> 00:47:00,332
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had that relationship with Rasool Allah ﷺ that he could tell him do and don’t.

587
00:47:01,957 --> 00:47:08,251
Their relationship was so close and it also shows you the humbleness of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

588
00:47:08,979 --> 00:47:11,290
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) comes and tells him don’t do that

589
00:47:12,225 --> 00:47:18,281
and Rasool Allah ﷺ accepts the opinion of Umar(عُمَر) with an open heart, and says; Then let them work.

590
00:47:19,430 --> 00:47:26,434
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to ear on the side of caution and not have people take things for granted.

591
00:47:27,255 --> 00:47:33,843
Don’t tell them that, let them work for it, even though they are going to Jannah(جنة) let them work for it.

592
00:47:36,267 --> 00:47:41,020
So, it tells you something about the personality of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) he was concerned for the Ummah(امة).

593
00:47:42,267 --> 00:47:48,672
You know, if it would have somebody else who was selfish alright fine I have glad tidings of Jannah(جنة) that’s it, I am happy.

594
00:47:49,184 --> 00:47:51,200
I don’t really care what will happen to the rest of the people.

595
00:47:51,240 --> 00:47:58,319
No! Umar(عُمَر) was thinking about what would happen, when Abu Hurairah(ابوهريرۃ) is going and telling the people this.

596
00:47:59,398 --> 00:48:03,053
Even though that was an occasion for him to be happy and satisfied

597
00:48:03,315 --> 00:48:07,521
no his mind immediately jumped to what is gonna happen with the Ummah(امة)?

598
00:48:07,894 --> 00:48:09,388
How are people are gonna take this?

599
00:48:10,293 --> 00:48:14,308
And that’s why we keep on saying that Umar(عُمَر) was the man for the Ummah(امة).

600
00:48:22,688 --> 00:48:28,705
In the beginning because Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه was a learned man, he was literate,

601
00:48:29,189 --> 00:48:35,785
 he wanted to swallow as much information as he could, so now he is in Madina there are Jewish neighbors.

602
00:48:35,904 --> 00:48:38,884
So why don’t I learn from their Books.?

603
00:48:39,346 --> 00:48:44,782
And Qur’an has said that they have received the Torah(تورات) and the Christians have received the Injeel(إنجيل).

604
00:48:44,960 --> 00:48:48,913
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wants to learn more about the religions of Allahعَزّ وجَلّ,

605
00:48:48,965 --> 00:48:51,746
So he is reading from a scroll of Torah(تورات).

606
00:48:52,095 --> 00:48:57,313
Rasool Allah ﷺ  sees it with him and the face of Rasool Allah ﷺ changes.

607
00:48:58,137 --> 00:49:01,480
And he can see that he was upset, and he said:

608
00:49:01,541 --> 00:49:04,017
 أَمُتَهَوِّكُوْنَ فِيْهَا يا اِبْنَ الخطاب؟

609
00:49:04,486 --> 00:49:09,066
Are you rushing into the things without thinking them true, son of Al-Khattab(ألخطاب)

610
00:49:09,923 --> 00:49:11,253
 وَالَّذِيْ نَفْسِيْ بِيَدِهْ

611
00:49:11,380 --> 00:49:14,954
In the name of Allah, Whom my soul, is in His hands.

612
00:49:15,767 --> 00:49:18,332
لَقَدْ جِـئْتُكُمْ بِهَا بِيْضَا نَقِيَّةْ

613
00:49:18,773 --> 00:49:22,363
I have brought you with the religion that is so clear, it’s like a white cloth.

614
00:49:24,148 --> 00:49:28,616
And if Musa(موسى) was alive today he would have to follow me.

615
00:49:31,445 --> 00:49:36,334
وَلَوْكَانَ مُوْسَى حَيًّا مَا وَسِعَه’ إِلَّا أَنْ يَتَّبِعَنِيْ

616
00:49:36,752 --> 00:49:39,703
If Musa(موسى) was alive he would have to follow me.

617
00:49:41,508 --> 00:49:45,645
You don’t need to go back to the old scripture everything that you need is in the Qur’an.

618
00:49:47,051 --> 00:49:48,650
It over rules everything before,

619
00:49:48,722 --> 00:49:49,832
مُهَيْمِنًا عَلَيْه

620
00:49:50,535 --> 00:49:52,165
it stands above everything else

621
00:49:53,871 --> 00:49:57,505
all of the truth that you need, all of the guidance that you need.

622
00:49:57,709 --> 00:49:59,342
مَّا فَرَّطْنَا فِى ٱلْكِتَٰبِ مِن شَىْءٍۢ

623
00:49:59,972 --> 00:50:02,024
The Book has not over looked anything.

624
00:50:02,829 --> 00:50:04,883
Everything that you need, you will find it in Qur’an.

625
00:50:07,197 --> 00:50:12,152
And this was an important lesson that was given to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and he learned the lesson very well.

626
00:50:12,252 --> 00:50:18,612
So later on when the Ummah(امة) was expanding and entering into the lands of learned men,

627
00:50:19,894 --> 00:50:26,100
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was very aware about the fact that they could bring in their former knowledge

628
00:50:26,523 --> 00:50:30,639
which could be tainted into Islam.

629
00:50:31,131 --> 00:50:37,457
So, he made sure that the people learned their knowledge from Qur’an and not from anything else.

630
00:50:39,578 --> 00:50:42,023
And we would see that in the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Umar(عُمَر),

631
00:50:42,063 --> 00:50:50,133
how he would design rules implemented to enforce the fact that your ilm(علم) should come from Qur’an and nothing else.

632
00:50:56,516 --> 00:50:59,220
UMAR(عُمَر) AND THE WIVES OF RASOOL ALLAH ﷺ,

633
00:51:05,023 --> 00:51:09,346
Ibn Abbasرضي الله عنه and this Hadith(حديث) is in Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم) and Masnad Imam Ahmad(مسنداِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

634
00:51:11,167 --> 00:51:12,114
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) said:

635
00:51:12,898 --> 00:51:19,528
There was something, that I wanted to ask Umar(عُمَر) and I waited for an entire year, until I asked him.

636
00:51:20,795 --> 00:51:24,720
He was afraid to ask Umar(عُمَر) the question.

637
00:51:26,128 --> 00:51:35,469
However, Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) because he was a scholar, given an inquisitive mind, he had to ask the question.

638
00:51:36,418 --> 00:51:37,321
لِسَانًا سَؤُوْلَأ

639
00:51:37,369 --> 00:51:39,935
I was given an inquisitive tongue.

640
00:51:41,802 --> 00:51:46,494
So one day they were traveling and he was pouring water on Umar(عُمَر) for his Wudu(وضؤ).

641
00:51:48,220 --> 00:51:49,838
Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) said:

642
00:51:50,371 --> 00:51:55,098
Who are the, two wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ whom Allaah talked about in Qur’an,

643
00:51:55,487 --> 00:51:59,360
إِنْ تَتُوبَا إِلَى اللَّهِ فَقَدْ صَغَتْ قُلُوبُكُمَا ۖ

644
00:52:00,423 --> 00:52:06,018
If you two turn in repentance to him your heart are indeed so inclined

645
00:52:06,854 --> 00:52:10,293
 but if you back up each other against him, against Rasool Allah ﷺ,

646
00:52:10,333 --> 00:52:16,340
truly Allah is his protector and Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) and every righteous one, among those, who believe

647
00:52:16,579 --> 00:52:18,806
and further more the Angels will back him up.

648
00:52:20,145 --> 00:52:22,121
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

649
00:52:22,146 --> 00:52:23,329
 وَاهَالَّكَ يَا اِبْنِ عَبَّاسْ

650
00:52:23,529 --> 00:52:28,123
Umar(عُمَر) wasn’t happy that Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) asked him this question, but he gave him the answer.

651
00:52:28,633 --> 00:52:29,184
 He said:

652
00:52:30,321 --> 00:52:34,755
"كُنَّا مَعْشَرَقُرَيْشْ قَوْمًا نَغْلِبٌ نِّسَآء "

653
00:52:35,962 --> 00:52:40,510
We the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were men, who had the upper hands over their women

654
00:52:41,633 --> 00:52:46,896
Our men had the upper hands over our women, our say goes.

655
00:52:47,950 --> 00:52:49,184
فَجِئْنَا قَوْمًا

656
00:52:49,433 --> 00:52:50,593
We came to Madina

657
00:52:50,867 --> 00:52:54,707
فَوَجَدْنَا قَوْمًا يَغْلِبُهُمْ نِسَأؤُهُمْ

658
00:52:55,305 --> 00:52:59,251
We found people in Madina their woman had the upper hand.

659
00:53:00,174 --> 00:53:03,451
فَطَفِقَ نِسَاؤُنَا يَتَعَلِّمْنَ مِنْ نِسَأئِهِمْ

660
00:53:03,843 --> 00:53:06,362
So, our women started learning from their women.

661
00:53:07,330 --> 00:53:10,955
Umar(عُمَر) is saying that in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) the men had the upper hand.

662
00:53:11,706 --> 00:53:16,817
In Madina, the women were quiet strong, so our women were learning from them.

663
00:53:18,356 --> 00:53:27,209
He said: One day I went back home and I was angry with my wife and she answered back to me.

664
00:53:29,103 --> 00:53:29,424
He said:

665
00:53:29,448 --> 00:53:30,356
 فَأَنْكَرْتُ ذَلِكْ

666
00:53:30,423 --> 00:53:33,514
So I was surprised what happened, how come, she is answering back.?

667
00:53:35,208 --> 00:53:37,899
She said: What you surprised that I am answering back to you?

668
00:53:39,178 --> 00:53:41,920
The wives of Rasool Allah ﷺ answer back to him.

669
00:53:44,028 --> 00:53:48,441
Not only that some would boycott him from morning to night.

670
00:53:49,754 --> 00:53:53,330
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) for him, this was News.

671
00:53:54,345 --> 00:54:02,994
So he rushes to his daughter Hafsa(حفصه), who was the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ, Umm Mo'mineen(ام المؤمنين), Hafsa رضي الله عنها

672
00:54:04,560 --> 00:54:09,375
- and he says: Do you answer back to Rasool Allah ﷺ, do you argue with him.?

673
00:54:09,867 --> 00:54:10,733
She said: Yes

674
00:54:11,453 --> 00:54:14,293
And sometimes we would boycott him from morning to night.

675
00:54:15,152 --> 00:54:19,318
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: You have lost! You are losers,

676
00:54:20,806 --> 00:54:26,901
Aren’t you afraid that Allah will become angry with you, because of the anger of His Messenger

677
00:54:30,350 --> 00:54:36,912
and then he said: Do not ever argue with Rasool Allah ﷺ or answer back to him,

678
00:54:37,865 --> 00:54:42,201
- and don’t ask him for anything and ask me whatever you want.

679
00:54:44,684 --> 00:54:45,579
And then he said:

680
00:54:48,108 --> 00:54:51,722
And don’t think that because Ayesha(عائشه) is doing it, you could do it.

681
00:54:52,258 --> 00:54:56,694
Ayesha(عائشه) is more beautiful than you and she is more beloved to Rasool Allah ﷺ then you.

682
00:55:00,314 --> 00:55:04,813
Because, the conspiracy was done by Ayesha(عائشه) and Hafsa(حفصه).

683
00:55:05,731 --> 00:55:10,279
So he is telling her that Ayesha(عائشه) may be could afford to do that, but you can’t, don’t do that!

684
00:55:12,329 --> 00:55:22,425
And then Umar(عُمَر) said: We heard that Ghassan(غسان), Ghassan(غسان) was a Arab Tribe loyal to the Romans,

685
00:55:23,274 --> 00:55:28,937
they were putting the horse shoes on, to attack us.

686
00:55:30,851 --> 00:55:36,809
We had that information already and we were waiting for that.

687
00:55:38,745 --> 00:55:42,856
He said: I was home when my Ansaari(انصاري) partner came to me

688
00:55:43,979 --> 00:55:46,212
and he said: Something big happened! I said:

689
00:55:46,247 --> 00:55:47,057
 اَجَاءَتْ غَسَّانْ

690
00:55:47,181 --> 00:55:48,087
Did Ghassan (غسان) come.?

691
00:55:48,203 --> 00:55:49,922
He said: No something worse than that.

692
00:55:50,695 --> 00:55:54,885
I told him what happened. He said: Rasool Allah ﷺ has divorced his wives.

693
00:55:55,947 --> 00:55:58,125
I said: That is what, I was afraid would happen.

694
00:55:59,417 --> 00:56:08,467
So I rushed to Madina, he was living on the out skirts of Madina I rushed to Hafsa(حفصه) and I saw her crying, she was sitting down crying.

695
00:56:08,959 --> 00:56:11,208
I told her: Did Rasool Allah ﷺ divorced you,

696
00:56:11,454 --> 00:56:12,601
She said: I don’t know!

697
00:56:13,169 --> 00:56:16,179
But he has boycotted us and he is in that room.

698
00:56:19,120 --> 00:56:26,899
So, I saw a servant of Rasool Ullah and I told him to ask for permission, for me to visit Rasool Ullah.

699
00:56:28,020 --> 00:56:31,866
He went in and came out and he said: I've mentioned your name to him and he didn’t answer.

700
00:56:34,245 --> 00:56:35,305
So, I left, I came back.

701
00:56:36,239 --> 00:56:38,763
I sought permission again the servant said:

702
00:56:39,152 --> 00:56:41,583
I mentioned your name, he didn’t answer,

703
00:56:42,366 --> 00:56:44,851
the third time, the same thing happened.

704
00:56:44,977 --> 00:56:48,237
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) walked away the servant then called him back.

705
00:56:50,333 --> 00:56:57,925
So, Umar(عُمَر) came in and he saw Rasool Allah ﷺ sitting and he was visibly upset.

706
00:57:00,314 --> 00:57:02,074
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه said:

707
00:57:02,105 --> 00:57:03,322
 أَطَّلَّقْتَ نِسَآءَ

708
00:57:03,503 --> 00:57:06,189
Did you divorce your wives?

709
00:57:07,784 --> 00:57:10,767
Rasool Allah ﷺ looked up to me and he said: No!

710
00:57:11,433 --> 00:57:12,788
I said: Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر)

711
00:57:15,814 --> 00:57:22,284
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) now wants to put Rasool Allah ﷺ at ease.

712
00:57:22,842 --> 00:57:27,681
So he is trying to start the conversation, he said: O Messenger of Allah,

713
00:57:28,659 --> 00:57:33,520
We the men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) used to have upper hand over our women

714
00:57:34,062 --> 00:57:38,844
and we come here to Madina, where the women are stronger then the men.

715
00:57:39,856 --> 00:57:49,819
So now our women are learning from their women and my wife is now talking back to me.

716
00:57:50,752 --> 00:57:52,265
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled.

717
00:57:57,278 --> 00:58:00,678
He said: I then went to Hafsa(حفصه)

718
00:58:01,444 --> 00:58:05,115
and I asked her is that what you do to Rasool Allah ﷺ and she said: Yes!

719
00:58:05,495 --> 00:58:09,088
We answer back to him, and sometimes we boycott him from morning to night.

720
00:58:09,398 --> 00:58:10,925
Rasool Allah ﷺ smiled again.

721
00:58:11,716 --> 00:58:13,873
So now Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said: Can I sit down?

722
00:58:14,620 --> 00:58:16,097
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Go ahead!

723
00:58:18,283 --> 00:58:19,684
And then Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said:

724
00:58:19,724 --> 00:58:25,176
I looked around the house of Rasool Allah ﷺ I couldn’t see anything that pleases the eye, there was nothing, no furniture

725
00:58:25,774 --> 00:58:32,561
and Rasool Allah ﷺ was sitting on a mattress of Haseer(حصير),

726
00:58:32,647 --> 00:58:44,462
Haseer(حصير) is Palm Leaves it's very harsh so it was leaving markings on the skin of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

727
00:58:45,702 --> 00:58:54,748
So I said: O Rasool Ullah, why don’t we ask Allah to give us like he is giving the Persians and the Romans,

728
00:58:55,130 --> 00:58:56,872
 when they don’t even believe in Allah.

729
00:58:59,185 --> 00:59:02,670
Rasool Allah ﷺ answered Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) and said:

730
00:59:06,038 --> 00:59:07,882
"أَفِيْ شَكٍّ أَنْتَ يَا ابن الخطاب؟"

731
00:59:08,055 --> 00:59:10,905
Are you having, any doubts O son of Khattab(الخطاب)?

732
00:59:11,393 --> 00:59:15,648
أُوْلئِكَ قَوْمٌ عُجِّلَتْ لَهُمْ طَيِّبَاتُهُمْ فِيْ الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا

733
00:59:16,239 --> 00:59:20,563
Those are people whom Allah is hastening their rewards in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

734
00:59:21,485 --> 00:59:25,333
Allah is giving them rewards in this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا) because in Akhira(آخرة) they will have nothing left.

735
00:59:25,872 --> 00:59:26,402
So I said:

736
00:59:26,473 --> 00:59:27,202
 اِسْتَغْفِرْلِيْ يارسول الله

737
00:59:27,226 --> 00:59:30,226
Ask Allah to forgive me, O Messenger of Allah.

738
00:59:32,644 --> 00:59:36,239
SOME LESSONS FROM THIS STORY:

739
00:59:36,331 --> 00:59:37,092
Number One,

740
00:59:39,064 --> 00:59:44,130
cultural differences exist in the demeanor of men and women.

741
00:59:45,474 --> 00:59:55,770
Men and women would have a different conduct of behavior in different cultures,

742
00:59:57,120 --> 01:00:01,021
so we saw how women were in Makkah more submissive,

743
01:00:01,430 --> 01:00:06,286
while in Madina they were stronger, you could even see that on the battle field.

744
01:00:07,077 --> 01:00:09,911
Nusayba Bint Ka'ab(انصيبة بنت كعب) for example an Ansaariya(انصاريه), was a fighter.

745
01:00:11,098 --> 01:00:16,024
That was the case with some of the other woman of Madina, they were tough, strong women.

746
01:00:17,891 --> 01:00:23,962
Similar could be said about some of the Bedouin women, they are strong by nature.

747
01:00:24,484 --> 01:00:26,257
So, cultural differences do exists.

748
01:00:26,323 --> 01:00:34,548
However, there are some Common Constant Islamic behaviors that should be applied cross culturally.

749
01:00:35,898 --> 01:00:37,999
That the husband is the head of the household.

750
01:00:38,341 --> 01:00:42,083
That is something that shouldn’t change from one culture to another.

751
01:00:43,368 --> 01:00:49,512
That the husband is to be obeyed by the wife, that is something that shouldn't changed from one culture to another.

752
01:00:50,618 --> 01:00:54,869
That the parents are to be respected, by their children, Shouldn’t change.

753
01:00:55,859 --> 01:00:59,999
That the young respect, the old that is something Islamic.

754
01:01:01,142 --> 01:01:06,987
So, these are things that are cross cultural and if a culture does not have them that culture should change.

755
01:01:08,518 --> 01:01:14,281
So, Islam does have some common teachings that are constant and should be applied by everyone.

756
01:01:14,703 --> 01:01:19,530
Over here we are just talking about difference in behavior

757
01:01:20,097 --> 01:01:23,580
but they are equally following the orders of Islam.

758
01:01:23,970 --> 01:01:27,481
I Don’t want sisters or brothers to get wrong message from this

759
01:01:27,540 --> 01:01:31,625
and they start arguing at home and say that’s how it was happening in Madina

760
01:01:32,809 --> 01:01:38,212
and wife start slapping her husband's around and all of that, and saying thing because that’s how the women of Madina were.

761
01:01:45,079 --> 01:01:48,482
Unless the husband is okay with that it's something else.

762
01:01:50,750 --> 01:01:52,486
Definitely Umar(عُمَر) wasn't okay with that.

763
01:01:58,086 --> 01:01:59,400
Tayyeb(طيب) In Sha Allah Ta'ala(إن شاء الله تعالى)

764
01:02:03,884 --> 01:02:05,195
We will carry on few minutes In Sha Allah Ta'ala(إن شاء الله تعالى).

765
01:02:05,241 --> 01:02:07,539
Some of the Fadhail of Umar(عُمَر), the next section is.

766
01:02:08,209 --> 01:02:11,743
THE FAZAIL(فضائل) OF UMAR BIN KHATTAB(عمرابن الخطاب), Some of his virtues:

767
01:02:16,558 --> 01:02:17,540
HIS KNOWLEDGE!

768
01:02:19,600 --> 01:02:24,653
 Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was knowledgeable, he was a scholar.

769
01:02:27,569 --> 01:02:30,088
In fact Rasool Allah ﷺ saw that in a dream,

770
01:02:32,009 --> 01:02:36,303
in Bukhari(بخاريْ) and Muslim(مسلم) Rasool Allah ﷺ  said:

771
01:02:37,379 --> 01:02:41,587
بَيْنَا أنَا نَائمٌ شَرِبْتُ يَعنِي اللَبَنٍ

772
01:02:42,074 --> 01:02:52,862
حَتَّى أَنظر ألى الرِّيَّ يَجْرِيْ فِيْ ظُهرِيْ ثُمَّ  نَاوَلْت ُعُمَرَ فَقَالُوا: فَمَا أَوَّلْتَهُ قَالَ: الْعِلْمَ

773
01:02:54,186 --> 01:03:00,487
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: While I was asleep, I saw in my dream that I was drinking milk

774
01:03:01,895 --> 01:03:07,941
and I drank so much of it that it started to flow from beneath my nails

775
01:03:10,153 --> 01:03:14,449
and then I gave the rest of the cup to Umar(عُمَر).

776
01:03:16,643 --> 01:03:20,562
They said: What do you interpret that, he said: Milk is knowledge.

777
01:03:22,087 --> 01:03:26,815
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ drank some much of that knowledge it was coming out of his fingers.

778
01:03:27,973 --> 01:03:31,704
And then he gave the rest to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), Knowledge of Prophet hood.

779
01:03:33,536 --> 01:03:37,475
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) had knowledge of Nabuwa(نبوة), of Prophet hood.

780
01:03:37,807 --> 01:03:42,675
The left overs the bottom of the cup was given to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

781
01:03:44,284 --> 01:03:49,629
A note here on interpretations of dreams, even the dreams of Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) needs to be interpreted

782
01:03:51,805 --> 01:03:54,356
because they asked Rasool Allah ﷺ about the interpretation of the dream.

783
01:03:55,241 --> 01:03:57,567
He said: Milk. Ibn Hajar As-Qalani(ابن حجر العسقلاني) says:

784
01:03:57,955 --> 01:04:03,088
وَجْه’ التَّعْبِيْرِ فِيْ الْحَدِيْثِ بِذَلِكَ مِنْ جِهَةِ اِشْتَرَاكِ الْلَبِنْ وَالْعِلْمْ فِيْ كَثْرَةٍ النَّفَعْ

785
01:04:03,454 --> 01:04:11,554
وَكَوْنَهُمَا سَبَبَا لِّلْصَلَاحْ، فَالْلَبَنُ لِلْغِذَاءِ الْبَدَنِيْ،وَالْعِلْمُ الِلّغِذَاءِ المَعْنَوِيْ

786
01:04:12,363 --> 01:04:18,888
He said: The reason why milk is knowledge is because of their benefit.

787
01:04:20,747 --> 01:04:25,821
Milk benefits the body and knowledge benefits the soul.

788
01:04:26,924 --> 01:04:30,991
So, that’s why milk represents the knowledge in this dream.

789
01:04:31,998 --> 01:04:36,398
And he also says and this is very important and interesting point. Ibn Hajar(ابن حجَر) says:

790
01:04:37,693 --> 01:04:45,934
وَالْمُرَادُ بِالْعِلْمِ هُنَا اَلْعِلْمِ بِسِيَاسَةِ النَّاسِ بِكِتَابِ الله وَسُنَّةِ نَبِيِّه صلى الله عليه وسلم

791
01:04:46,584 --> 01:04:52,267
And what is meant by knowledge here is the knowledge of the administration of the people

792
01:04:52,602 --> 01:04:55,985
in accordance to the Book of Allah and Sunnah(سنة) of His Messenger.

793
01:04:57,215 --> 01:05:01,442
We have developed a certain concept of what Sharia’ah(شريعه) knowledge is.

794
01:05:02,490 --> 01:05:11,757
If you are able to quote the narrations off hand from the top of your head easily this man is a Sheikh(شيخ)

795
01:05:13,073 --> 01:05:16,142
If you are able to speak very eloquently you are a scholar,

796
01:05:16,447 --> 01:05:17,825
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) what a scholar.

797
01:05:19,674 --> 01:05:20,992
Ibn Hajar(ابن حجَر) is saying,

798
01:05:21,032 --> 01:05:26,404
the ilm(علم) here is the ability of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to administer the Ummah(امة)

799
01:05:28,294 --> 01:05:31,874
by the Book of Allahعَزّ وجَلّ and Sunnah(سنة) of Muhammad ﷺ.

800
01:05:32,424 --> 01:05:37,972
It was referring to the ability of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) as a statesman, when he was Khalifah(خليفه)

801
01:05:39,024 --> 01:05:41,216
and that is the knowledge that benefited the Ummah(امة).

802
01:05:42,101 --> 01:05:44,415
There could be someone who has a lot of knowledge,

803
01:05:45,717 --> 01:05:50,927
wrote memorization, they memorize all the books but they have no clue how to use it, how to apply it?

804
01:05:53,001 --> 01:05:58,945
They don’t have the Fiqh(فقه) of Al-Waqia(الواقع) the understanding of the reality of the world today.

805
01:05:59,104 --> 01:06:02,848
 They are not in the field, and that's why Ibn Khaldoon(ابن خلدون) says;

806
01:06:03,199 --> 01:06:12,909
That many of the people, who are called scholars tend to be very far away and unable to deal with the realities of people,

807
01:06:13,235 --> 01:06:17,132
in their political life, in the political realities of life.

808
01:06:18,542 --> 01:06:20,753
Because they are only living with their books.

809
01:06:21,670 --> 01:06:25,202
But with the knowledge of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) it was a knowledge that was applied in the field.

810
01:06:26,159 --> 01:06:31,730
He wasn’t just sitting in the institute studying and giving off Fatawa(فتاوى) on the phone or on the Mic.

811
01:06:33,166 --> 01:06:35,173
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was living with the Ummah(امة).

812
01:06:36,495 --> 01:06:38,995
He was leading the Ummah(امة), he was suffering with the Ummah(امة).

813
01:06:39,704 --> 01:06:44,390
He was pleased what pleases them and displeased what would displease them,

814
01:06:46,033 --> 01:06:54,954
so be careful in using this word Ilm(علم) don’t throw it around carelessly, such person is a Mufti(مفتي), such person is scholar.

815
01:06:57,083 --> 01:07:06,801
The Ulama(علماء) are the ones who know how to benefit the people through the Ilm(علم) of Allah in Qur’an and in the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

816
01:07:08,515 --> 01:07:13,719
And these could be people who don’t memorize a lot of opinions of Fiqh(فقه).

817
01:07:14,428 --> 01:07:17,817
You would ask them what did Abu Haneefa(ابو حنيفه)  say on this, or what did Ashafi'e(شافعي) say on that?

818
01:07:17,976 --> 01:07:24,828
Or what did Qadhi Iyyadh(قاضي عياض) say, or what did Al-izza Bin Abdussalam(العزة بن عبدالسلام) say, they wouldn’t know that.

819
01:07:27,162 --> 01:07:30,526
But they know what is needed for that situation, they know it very well.

820
01:07:30,628 --> 01:07:34,449
They know how to apply the Ayaat(آيات) and the Ahadith(احاديث) that they've learned.

821
01:07:34,619 --> 01:07:36,723
They know how to apply them in the reality of people.

822
01:07:38,290 --> 01:07:41,311
And that’s why Allahعَزّ وجَلّ says about for example Daud(داؤد)

823
01:07:41,549 --> 01:07:43,261
 واتيناهم حكم وعلماً

824
01:07:43,491 --> 01:07:45,176
We have given him Hukm(حكم) and Ilm(علم).

825
01:07:47,427 --> 01:07:51,261
Ilm(علم) and Hukm(حكم), Hukm(حكم) is the good Judgment.

826
01:07:53,772 --> 01:07:59,105
A judge could have the information right there but he doesn’t know how to use it.

827
01:08:01,436 --> 01:08:04,604
The ability to use it, is Hukm(حكم), the good Judgment.

828
01:08:07,311 --> 01:08:09,674
Once a woman came to the Halaqah(حلقه) of Abu Haneefa(ابو حنيفه).

829
01:08:10,985 --> 01:08:13,917
Al-Imam Abu Haneefa(امام ابو حنيفه), she asked a question

830
01:08:14,802 --> 01:08:20,517
she didn’t ask the question to Abu Haneefa(ابو حنيفه), she asked it to a scholar of Hadith(حديث) who was sitting in that circle.

831
01:08:21,774 --> 01:08:28,020
Because the Majlis(مجلس) the circle of Abu Haneefa(ابو حنيفه) was a circle of scholars.

832
01:08:29,133 --> 01:08:31,030
He had scholars sitting with him.

833
01:08:31,846 --> 01:08:35,073
It was more of a council of Fiqh(فقه) than a study circle.

834
01:08:35,616 --> 01:08:38,594
That's one of the unique things with Abu Haneefa(ابو حنيفه),

835
01:08:39,554 --> 01:08:45,285
you don’t call his students, students you call them As-Haab(اصحاب) friends, companions

836
01:08:46,354 --> 01:08:48,306
because they were scholars like him.

837
01:08:48,836 --> 01:08:54,819
He had scholars in language, scholars in Hadith(حديث),  scholars in Fiqh(فقه), so they would consult each other.

838
01:08:55,416 --> 01:08:59,702
So, this woman comes to one of the scholars and she asks him a question, he didn’t know the answer.

839
01:09:00,674 --> 01:09:03,834
Abu Haneefa(ابو حنيفه) said: I know the answer, he gave her the answer.

840
01:09:03,891 --> 01:09:05,967
 So the scholar of Hadith(حديث) said: How did you know the answer?

841
01:09:06,302 --> 01:09:09,265
He said: I knew it by the Hadith(حديث) you just quoted a while ago.

842
01:09:10,185 --> 01:09:14,413
You are the one who quoted the Daleel(دليل) for me I didn’t know the evidence for it, until you quoted it.

843
01:09:15,281 --> 01:09:16,650
But he didn’t know how to use it.

844
01:09:16,952 --> 01:09:18,999
Imam(اِمَام) Abu Haneefa(ابو حنيفه) knew how to use it.

845
01:09:36,045 --> 01:09:39,028
Tayyib(طيب) we will carry on In sha Allah(اِن شاء الله) tomorrow night

846
01:09:39,234 --> 01:09:43,070
with the rest of the Fadhail(فضائل) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

847
01:09:43,763 --> 01:09:48,013
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

848
01:09:48,131 --> 01:09:56,407
IT SHUDDERS IN PAIN FREELY, MY CHASITY, MY MODESTY!

849
01:09:56,531 --> 01:10:02,707
OH MUSLIM, YOU SAW, MY INJURY AND THE INJURY OF MY PRIDE.

